      "retrieval_hit": true,
      "citation_hit": true,
      "fact_hit": true,
      "answer": "MATAF_01 has been above 90% for 12 minutes, which exceeds the **5-minute sustained threshold** for CRITICAL escalation defined in SOP-CS-004 §3.1 [5, SOP-CS-004]. The zone is therefore in **CRITICAL (90–94%)** status and the following procedure applies:\n\n1. **SOC Controller assumes control of the zone** (already required at the 5-minute mark) [1, SOP-CS-011].\n2. **Inflow must be stopped entirely**; contraflow egress opened; arriving flow diverted to an alternate zone [3, SOP-CS-011].\n3. **Diversion at CRITICAL is authorised by the SOC Controller** [4, SOP-CS-011].\n4. **Duty Operations Director and Civil Defence Liaison must be notified immediately** (the 95% single-reading trigger also requires immediate notification, but at 90% sustained the Duty Operations Director is already required to be notified) [1, SOP-CS-011]; [3, SOP-CS-011].\n\nIf any of these actions (SOC control, inflow stop, diversion, notifications) have not yet occurred, treat it as a **reportable failure under SOP-OPS-020** [1, SOP-CS-011].",
