      "retrieval_hit": true,
      "citation_hit": true,
      "fact_hit": true,
      "answer": "**First three steps (in this order) when a child is reported missing at MASAA_L2:**\n\n1. **Contain the reporter and record the description.** Do not let the family member walk away to search. Record: name, age, height, clothing colours, footwear, distinguishing features, language spoken, wristband or group identifier, and the exact location and time last seen. [1, SOP-SEC-007]\n\n2. **Raise the request immediately as LOST_PERSON P2** in the operations platform and broadcast the description on the sector radio channel. The broadcast must happen within the first minute — before any search begins. A missing child is always P2 or higher; it is never P3. [1, SOP-SEC-007] [2, SOP-SEC-007]\n\n3. **Seal the immediate area and search outward from the last known point.** Marshals at the zone's exits hold position and observe rather than joining the search. A child moves outward from where they were lost; staff who leave the exits to search inward let them past. [1, SOP-SEC-007]\n\nOnly after these three steps are complete does the wider search escalate. [1, SOP-SEC-007]",
