      "retrieval_hit": true,
      "citation_hit": true,
      "fact_hit": true,
      "answer": "The baseline servicing interval for a water station is **every 4 hours** under normal operations. This interval shortens based on conditions:\n\n- **Every 2 hours** when the zone is at ELEVATED or HIGH utilisation, or during Heat Level 1–2 (WBGT 28–31.9 °C) [2, SOP-SAN-003]\n- **Every hour** during Heat Level 3–4 (WBGT ≥ 32 °C) [2, SOP-SAN-003]\n- **Every 6 hours** overnight (23:00–04:00) under normal heat [2, SOP-SAN-003]\n\nA servicing visit that finds a station below 25% capacity halves that station's interval until two consecutive visits find it above 50% [2, SOP-SAN-003].",
